{"type":"event","event":{"type":"tool_completed","toolCallId":"call_c0c517744b6c46a48557439a","toolName":"read_file","result":[{"type":"text","text":"Read 1/1 file, 1174 lines\n1: (ns dao.stream.remote\n2:   \"DaoStream remote: any stream, reachable as itself\n3:    (docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md, sections 2 through 2.5).\n4: \n5:    A peer that holds a handle answers the handle's own operations as\n6:    data over a channel; a peer at the other end holds a handle -- the\n7:    reflection -- whose operations are those questions asked across the\n8:    channel, with the source's outcome maps returned verbatim.\n9: \n10:    `mirror-step` is the pure answering step a peer runs over a channel\n11:    against its table. It never constructs, parses or rewrites a cursor,\n12:    an anchor or an outcome, and its steps 1 to 4 are its only contacts\n13:    with the entry's handle: every cursor, next and append! runs through\n14:    `dao.stream.middleware/apply-request` with the channel context, so\n15:    nothing bypasses the entry's middleware or its declared surface.\n16:    `attacher` is the composition's :dao.stream/attach entry for\n17:    :dao.stream/remote descriptors; it keeps one link per channel\n18:    descriptor, shared by every reflection through that channel, and\n19:    answers ok at once -- the contract's deferred remote confirmation.\n20:    There is no :dao.stream/create entry: attaching through this\n21:    transport never creates.\n22: \n23:    A name is lookup data and never a :dao.stream/identity. A peer's\n24:    composition may hold, beside its table, a name map {name identity};\n25:    a named descriptor request carries :dao.stream.remote/name in place\n26:    of :dao.stream/identity and the mirror answers the mapped entry's\n27:    own identity and surface. `links` is the asking side: the attach\n28:    entry and `resolve` over the same per-channel links, so a name is\n29:    resolved and its stream then attached through one link.\"\n30:   (:require [dao.stream :as stream]\n31:             [dao.stream.middleware :as middleware]))\n32: \n33: \n34: ;; =============================================================================\n35: ;; Wire shapes (2.1)\n36: ;; =============================================================================\n37: \n38: (def ^:private wire-ops\n39:   \"The four wire operations. close! never crosses -- the mirror holds\n40:    nothing per remote party to close and the owner's close is never\n41:    remote -- and attach! never crosses, because it consumes a\n42:    descriptor and produces a local handle.\"\n43:   #{:dao.stream/descriptor :dao.stream/cursor :dao.stream/next\n44:     :dao.stream/append!})\n45: \n46: \n47: (def ^:private protocol-errors\n48:   \"The three protocol errors, one answer shape for every operation,\n49:    a key instead of an outcome map because no operation's outcome set\n50:    can carry them.\"\n51:   #{:dao.stream.remote/not-found\n52:     :dao.stream.remote/no-surface\n53:     :dao.stream.remote/oversize})\n54: \n55: \n56: (defn- named?\n57:   \"True when the map `v` carries a name: a named request, or the\n58:    answer to one.\"\n59:   [v]\n60:   (contains? v :dao.stream.remote/name))\n61: \n62: \n63: (defn- well-formed-request?\n64:   \"True when `v` is a well-formed request: a map naming its identity\n65:    and one of the four wire ops, carrying an args vector and the\n66:    asker-minted id; or a named request, which carries a name in place\n67:    of the identity and may ride the descriptor op only, with empty\n68:    args. A request that carries an identity is an identity request\n69:    whatever else it carries; a named request with any other op, or\n70:    with args that are not empty, is malformed. Anything else is\n71:    dropped as malformed wire input.\"\n72:   [v]\n73:   (and (map? v)\n74:        (vector? (:dao.stream.remote/args v))\n75:        (contains? v :dao.stream.remote/id)\n76:        (if (contains? v :dao.stream/identity)\n77:          (contains? wire-ops (:dao.stream.remote/op v))\n78:          (and (named? v)\n79:               (= :dao.stream/descriptor (:dao.stream.remote/op v))\n80:               (empty? (:dao.stream.remote/args v))))))\n81: \n82: \n83: (defn- well-formed-answer?\n84:   \"True when `v` is a well-formed answer: a map carrying the id and\n85:    the identity and either a protocol error or an outcome map. The\n86:    answer to a named request carries the name; its not-found error\n87:    carries the name and no identity, because an unmapped name names no\n88:    stream, and so does the oversize error that replaces an answer that\n89:    carried none.\"\n90:   [v]\n91:   (and (map? v)\n92:        (contains? v :dao.stream.remote/id)\n93:        (or (contains? v :dao.stream/identity)\n94:            (and (named? v)\n95:                 (contains? #{:dao.stream.remote/not-found\n96:                              :dao.stream.remote/oversize}\n97:                            (:dao.stream.remote/error v))))\n98:        (or (contains? protocol-errors (:dao.stream.remote/error v))\n99:            (stream/outcome-map? v))))\n100: \n101: \n102: (defn- required-surface\n103:   \"The declared surface `op` needs, under the fixed mapping: cursor\n104:    and next need :reader, append! needs :writer, descriptor needs no\n105:    surface and is always answerable.\"\n106:   [op]\n107:   (case op\n108:     (:dao.stream/cursor :dao.stream/next) :reader\n109:     :dao.stream/append! :writer\n110:     nil))\n111: \n112: \n113: (defn- error-answer\n114:   \"The protocol-error answer shape, with the id and identity the\n115:    request carried.\"\n116:   [identity id e]\n117:   {:dao.stream/identity identity\n118:    :dao.stream.remote/id id\n119:    :dao.stream.remote/error e})\n120: \n121: \n122: ;; =============================================================================\n123: ;; The mirror step (2.3)\n124: ;; =============================================================================\n125: \n126: (defn- valid-budget?\n127:   \"True when the request carries the optional next-only budget as a\n128:    positive integer. Anything else ignores the budget, which is always\n129:    correct for a mirror.\"\n130:   [req]\n131:   (let [k (:dao.stream.remote/budget req)]\n132:     (and (integer? k) (pos? k))))\n133: \n134: \n135: (defn- chase\n136:   \"The budget chase: `outcome` is an ok from next; follow the successor\n137:    cursor through the same apply-request path at most k - 1 further\n138:    times, collecting the further outcome maps in order. The vector ends\n139:    at and includes the first non-ok outcome, so blocked, end and gap\n140:    reach the reader with the source's own recovery cursor.\"\n141:   [h ctx k outcome]\n142:   (loop [more [] cur (:dao.stream/cursor outcome) n 1]\n143:     (if (or (>= n k) (nil? cur))\n144:       more\n145:       (let [r (middleware/apply-request h ctx\n146:                                         {:dao.stream.remote/op\n147:                                          :dao.stream/next\n148:                                          :dao.stream.remote/args [cur]})]\n149:         (if (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n150:           (recur (conj more r) (:dao.stream/cursor r) (inc n))\n151:           (conj more r))))))\n152: \n153: \n154: (defn- write-answer!\n155:   \"Append one answer value toward the asker. A value the channel cannot\n156:    carry (invalid-value) is answered with the oversize protocol error\n157:    in place of that element, the read not skipped and no cursor\n158:    advanced past it; any other refused write leaves the request\n159:    unanswered. Returns the writer's outcome of the last append.\"\n160:   [chan-writer answer]\n161:   (let [r (stream/append! chan-writer answer)]\n162:     (if (= :dao.stream/invalid-value (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n163:       (stream/append! chan-writer\n164:                       (assoc (select-keys answer [:dao.stream/identity\n165:                                                   :dao.stream.remote/id\n166:                                                   :dao.stream.remote/name])\n167:                              :dao.stream.remote/error\n168:                              :dao.stream.remote/oversize))\n169:       r)))\n170: \n171: \n172: (defn- descriptor-answer\n173:   \"The descriptor answer of a table entry: the entry's handle's own\n174:    descriptor outcome, with the id, the served identity and the\n175:    entry's declared surface.\"\n176:   [entry identity id]\n177:   (-> (stream/descriptor (:handle entry))\n178:       (assoc :dao.stream.remote/id id\n179:              :dao.stream/identity identity\n180:              :dao.stream.remote/surface (:surface entry))))\n181: \n182: \n183: (defn- answer-named!\n184:   \"The mirror's step 0 for one well-formed named request: look the\n185:    name up in the name map and the identity it maps to in the table.\n186:    An unmapped name, and a name mapped to an identity the table lacks,\n187:    are answered not-found with the name and no identity. Otherwise the\n188:    answer is the descriptor answer of the mapped entry -- its own\n189:    identity, its declared surface -- with the name echoed. The name\n190:    never rides :dao.stream/identity. Returns the writer's outcome.\"\n191:   [table names chan-writer req]\n192:   (let [n (:dao.stream.remote/name req)\n193:         id (:dao.stream.remote/id req)\n194:         identity (when (map? names) (get names n))\n195:         entry (when (and (map? names) (contains? names n))\n196:                 (get table identity))]\n197:     (write-answer!\n198:       chan-writer\n199:       (if-not entry\n200:         {:dao.stream.remote/id id\n201:          :dao.stream.remote/name n\n202:          :dao.stream.remote/error :dao.stream.remote/not-found}\n203:         (assoc (descriptor-answer entry identity id)\n204:                :dao.stream.remote/name n)))))\n205: \n206: \n207: (defn- answer!\n208:   \"The mirror's steps 1 to 4 for one well-formed request: look the\n209:    identity up in the table (not-found); check the op against the\n210:    entry's declared surface under the fixed mapping (no-surface);\n211:    answer descriptor from the entry's handle directly, adding the\n212:    declared surface, and apply cursor, next and append! through\n213:    apply-request with the channel context; append the answer with the\n214:    id and identity. For next with a budget k, and an ok first outcome,\n215:    the chase places the further outcomes under more, k clamped to the\n216:    local chase-max when one is given. Returns the writer's outcome.\"\n217:   [table chan-writer channel chase-max req]\n218:   (let [identity (:dao.stream/identity req)\n219:         id (:dao.stream.remote/id req)\n220:         op (:dao.stream.remote/op req)\n221:         entry (get table identity)]\n222:     (if-not entry\n223:       (write-answer! chan-writer\n224:                      (error-answer identity id\n225:                                    :dao.stream.remote/not-found))\n226:       (let [h (:handle entry)]\n227:         (if (= :dao.stream/descriptor op)\n228:           (write-answer! chan-writer (descriptor-answer entry identity id))\n229:           (if-not (contains? (into #{} (:surface entry))\n230:                              (required-surface op))\n231:             (write-answer! chan-writer\n232:                            (error-answer identity id\n233:                                          :dao.stream.remote/no-surface))\n234:             (let [ctx {:dao.stream.remote/channel channel}\n235:                   outcome (middleware/apply-request h ctx req)\n236:                   more (when (and (= :dao.stream/next op)\n237:                                   (valid-budget? req)\n238:                                   (= :dao.stream/ok\n239:                                      (:dao.stream/outcome outcome)))\n240:                          (let [k (:dao.stream.remote/budget req)]\n241:                            (chase h ctx\n242:                                   (if chase-max (min k chase-max) k)\n243:                                   outcome)))\n244:                   answer (cond-> (assoc outcome\n245:                                         :dao.stream.remote/id id\n246:                                         :dao.stream/identity identity)\n247:                            (seq more) (assoc :dao.stream.remote/more\n248:                                              more))]\n249:               (write-answer! chan-writer answer))))))))\n250: \n251: \n252: (defn- pos-int-or-nil?\n253:   [x]\n254:   (or (nil? x) (and (integer? x) (pos? x))))\n255: \n256: \n257: (defn mirror-step\n258:   \"The pure step a peer runs over a channel to answer requests against\n259:    its table: `(mirror-step table chan-reader cursor chan-writer) ->\n260:    cursor'`. For each request read from chan-reader at `cursor`, in\n261:    order, the four steps of 2.3 run; the mirror holds no state between\n262:    calls beyond the returned cursor. A value that is neither a\n263:    well-formed request nor a well-formed answer is dropped as malformed\n264:    wire input. The step stops when the channel reader answers blocked\n265:    or end; a gap adopts the reader's own recovery cursor, the lost wire\n266:    values being lost. The mirror never constructs, parses or rewrites\n267:    a cursor, an anchor or an outcome: the served stream is the\n268:    original, its cursors, its positions, its gap, its end.\n269: \n270:    The five-argument form takes the composition's name map `names`,\n271:    {name identity}, each value a key of `table`: a named descriptor\n272:    request is answered from it (step 0). Without a name map every\n273:    name is unmapped.\n274: \n275:    The six-argument form takes `bounds`, nil or a map of optional\n276:    positive integers: :dao.stream.remote/mirror-budget bounds the\n277:    wire values read per call -- each ok read, well-formed or not, and\n278:    each gap counts one -- returning the cursor to continue from;\n279:    :dao.stream.remote/chase-budget clamps a peer-requested next\n280:    budget. Any other bounds is a composition error. A writer that\n281:    answers full on the answer of a descriptor, cursor, next or named\n282:    descriptor request stops the step at the cursor preceding that\n283:    request, so it is re-read and re-answered next call; a full on an\n284:    append! answer is dropped, the source append having run.\"\n285:   ([table chan-reader cursor chan-writer]\n286:    (mirror-step table nil chan-reader cursor chan-writer nil))\n287:   ([table names chan-reader cursor chan-writer]\n288:    (mirror-step table names chan-reader cursor chan-writer nil))\n289:   ([table names chan-reader cursor chan-writer bounds]\n290:    (when-not (or (nil? bounds)\n291:                  (and (map? bounds)\n292:                       (every? pos-int-or-nil? (vals bounds))))\n293:      (throw (ex-info \"invalid DaoStream remote mirror bounds\"\n294:                      {:bounds bounds})))\n295:    (let [channel (:dao.stream/identity (stream/descriptor chan-reader))\n296:          budget (:dao.stream.remote/mirror-budget bounds)\n297:          chase-max (:dao.stream.remote/chase-budget bounds)]\n298:      (loop [cursor cursor remaining budget]\n299:        (if (and remaining (zero? remaining))\n300:          cursor\n301:          (let [r (stream/next chan-reader cursor)\n302:                remaining' (when remaining (dec remaining))]\n303:            (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n304:              :dao.stream/ok\n305:              (let [v (:dao.stream/value r)\n306:                    w (when (well-formed-request? v)\n307:                        (if (contains? v :dao.stream/identity)\n308:                          (answer! table chan-writer channel chase-max v)\n309:                          (answer-named! table names chan-writer v)))]\n310:                (if (and (= :dao.stream/full (:dao.stream/outcome w))\n311:                         (not= :dao.stream/append!\n312:                               (:dao.stream.remote/op v)))\n313:                  cursor\n314:                  (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) remaining')))\n315:              :dao.stream/blocked cursor\n316:              :dao.stream/end cursor\n317:              :dao.stream/gap (recur (:dao.stream/cursor r) remaining')\n318:              cursor)))))))\n319: \n320: \n321: ;; =============================================================================\n322: ;; The link (2.4, 2.5)\n323: ;; =============================================================================\n324: \n325: (defn- new-link\n326:   \"One link per channel descriptor, shared by every reflection through\n327:    that channel. A link holds the channel writer; the channel reader\n328:    and the link's own cursor on it; the outstanding request ids with\n329:    the request each was sent for; the attach descriptor probes the\n330:    writer has refused, kept unsent with the reflection each was sent\n331:    for; filed answers keyed by id; the more outcomes installed at\n332:    their served identity and the cursor that precedes each; an\n333:    optional event writer; and the policy data -- the resend-after k,\n334:    the budget k stamped on next requests, and the bounds on reads per\n335:    drain, on outstanding plus kept requests and on filed plus\n336:    installed answers, all composition data.\"\n337:   [cd chan policy]\n338:   (atom {:channel cd\n339:          :reader (:reader chan)\n340:          :writer (:writer chan)\n341:          :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor\n342:                    (stream/cursor (:reader chan) :dao.stream/oldest))\n343:          :outstanding {}\n344:          :pending {}\n345:          :filed {}\n346:          :filed-cursors {}\n347:          :filed-seq 0\n348:          :events (:dao.stream.remote/events policy)\n349:          :resend-after (:dao.stream.remote/resend-after policy)\n350:          :budget (:dao.stream.remote/budget policy)\n351:          :drain-budget (:dao.stream.remote/drain-budget policy)\n352:          :max-outstanding (:dao.stream.remote/max-outstanding policy)\n353:          :max-filed (:dao.stream.remote/max-filed policy)\n354:          :next-id 0\n355:          :channel-gone? false}))\n356: \n357: \n358: (defn- mint-id!\n359:   \"The next asker-minted id, unique per channel.\"\n360:   [link]\n361:   (let [n (:next-id @link)]\n362:     (swap! link assoc :next-id (inc n))\n363:     n))\n364: \n365: \n366: (defn- emit!\n367:   \"Append one event to the link's event writer when one is composed;\n368:    without an event writer the event is dropped.\"\n369:   [link v]\n370:   (when-some [w (:events @link)]\n371:     (stream/append! w v)))\n372: \n373: \n374: (defn- register!\n375:   \"Record `req` as outstanding under its id, with the request it was\n376:    sent for, its ask count, and the reflection that sent it.\"\n377:   [link refl req]\n378:   (let [id (:dao.stream.remote/id req)]\n379:     (swap! link assoc-in [:outstanding id]\n380:            {:req req :asks 0 :reflection refl})\n381:     (swap! refl update :ids conj id)))\n382: \n383: \n384: (defn- stamped-budget\n385:   \"The budget a next request carries: the link's budget, no more than\n386:    max-filed when both are composed -- the link could retain no more\n387:    outcomes than that, so asking for more would only be dropped.\"\n388:   [link]\n389:   (let [{:keys [budget max-filed]} @link]\n390:     (if (and (integer? budget) max-filed)\n391:       (min budget max-filed)\n392:       budget)))\n393: \n394: \n395: (defn- wire-request\n396:   \"One request map for the channel, its id asker-minted; a next\n397:    request carries the link's stamped budget when one is composed.\"\n398:   [link refl op args]\n399:   (let [k (stamped-budget link)]\n400:     (cond-> {:dao.stream/identity (:identity @refl)\n401:              :dao.stream.remote/op op\n402:              :dao.stream.remote/args args\n403:              :dao.stream.remote/id (mint-id! link)}\n404:       (and (= :dao.stream/next op) (some? k))\n405:       (assoc :dao.stream.remote/budget k))))\n406: \n407: \n408: (defn- room?\n409:   \"True when the link holds fewer than max-outstanding requests,\n410:    outstanding or kept, not counting `id` itself, or has no such bound.\n411:    Sends and kept probes are both admitted only with room, so\n412:    outstanding plus kept never exceeds the bound, and a kept probe's\n413:    own retry -- which excludes itself -- always has room.\"\n414:   [link id]\n415:   (let [{:keys [max-outstanding outstanding pending]} @link]\n416:     (or (nil? max-outstanding)\n417:         (< (+ (count outstanding) (count (dissoc pending id)))\n418:            max-outstanding))))\n419: \n420: \n421: (defn- send!\n422:   \"Append `req` to the channel writer, unless the link has no room\n423:    for it: that send is refused locally as though the writer answered\n424:    full, nothing crossing.\"\n425:   [link req]\n426:   (if (room? link (:dao.stream.remote/id req))\n427:     (stream/append! (:writer @link) req)\n428:     {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/full}))\n429: \n430: \n431: (defn- send-request!\n432:   \"Append one request map to the channel writer and register it as\n433:    outstanding only when the writer accepted the send: a send the\n434:    writer refuses with full leaves the request unsent and nothing\n435:    outstanding, so the operation answers as though unanswered and the\n436:    next ask sends again. A send over max-outstanding is refused the\n437:    same way (send!). An attach descriptor probe refused with full is\n438:    kept on the link instead, unsent, one retry per drain until a send\n439:    is accepted -- when the link has room for it; otherwise it waits on\n440:    its own reflection, unadmitted, and that reflection's next operation\n441:    offers it again (admit-probe!). Returns the writer's outcome.\"\n442:   [link refl req]\n443:   (let [r (send! link req)\n444:         id (:dao.stream.remote/id req)]\n445:     (cond\n446:       (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n447:       (do (register! link refl req)\n448:           (swap! link update :pending dissoc id)\n449:           (swap! refl dissoc :probe))\n450: \n451:       (and (= :dao.stream/full (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n452:            (= :dao.stream/descriptor (:dao.stream.remote/op req)))\n453:       (if (room? link id)\n454:         (do (swap! link assoc-in [:pending id]\n455:                    {:req req :reflection refl})\n456:             (swap! refl dissoc :probe))\n457:         (swap! refl assoc :probe req)))\n458:     r))\n459: \n460: \n461: (defn- count-ask!\n462:   \"Count one further ask of the outstanding request `id`; on reaching\n463:    the link's resend-after k, re-send it once -- the same id, a\n464:    duplicate of an idempotent operation, which recomputes the same or a\n465:    later, equally true answer -- and start counting afresh. append! is\n466:    never re-sent: it never stays outstanding beyond its send.\"\n467:   [link id]\n468:   (when-some [entry (get (:outstanding @link) id)]\n469:     (let [k (:resend-after @link)\n470:           asks (inc (:asks entry))]\n471:       (swap! link assoc-in [:outstanding id :asks] asks)\n472:       (when (and (integer? k) (pos? k) (<= k asks))\n473:         (stream/append! (:writer @link) (:req entry))\n474:         (swap! link assoc-in [:outstanding id :asks] 0)))))\n475: \n476: \n477: (defn- outstanding-for\n478:   \"The id of the link's outstanding request for `op` with `arg` sent by\n479:    `refl`, if any; the request each outstanding id was sent for makes\n480:    the correlation.\"\n481:   [link refl op arg]\n482:   (when-some [[id _]\n483:               (first\n484:                 (filter (fn [[_ e]]\n485:                           (let [r (:req e)]\n486:                             (and (= refl (:reflection e))\n487:                                  (= op (:dao.stream.remote/op r))\n488:                                  (= arg (first\n489:                                           (:dao.stream.remote/args r))))))\n490:                         (:outstanding @link)))]\n491:     id))\n492: \n493: \n494: (defn- filed-for\n495:   \"The first filed answer for `op` with `arg` sent by `refl`, in id\n496:    order, as [id entry]. A filed answer keeps the request it was sent\n497:    for and the reflection that sent it -- an answer belongs to the\n498:    operation that caused it -- so it is found whether or not its\n499:    outstanding id was abandoned.\"\n500:   [link refl op arg]\n501:   (let [filed (:filed @link)]\n502:     (when-some [id\n503:                 (first\n504:                   (filter (fn [i]\n505:                             (let [e (get filed i)\n506:                                   r (:req e)]\n507:                               (and (= refl (:reflection e))\n508:                                    (= op (:dao.stream.remote/op r))\n509:                                    (= arg (first\n510:                                             (:dao.stream.remote/args r))))))\n511:                           (sort (keys filed))))]\n512:       [id (get filed id)])))\n513: \n514: \n515: (defn- bare-outcome\n516:   \"The source's own outcome map, verbatim: the correlation keys the\n517:    answer envelope added are removed, nothing else.\"\n518:   [ans]\n519:   (dissoc ans :dao.stream.remote/id :dao.stream/identity))\n520: \n521: \n522: (defn- translated\n523:   \"A filed protocol error at the reflection: transport-error with the\n524:    error's name as the reason. not-found marks the reflection gone at\n525:    filing; no-surface and oversize mark nothing.\"\n526:   [e]\n527:   {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n528:    :dao.stream.remote/reason e})\n529: \n530: \n531: (defn- learn!\n532:   \"The attach probe's ok: record the source's descriptor and declared\n533:    surface, plus :closable.\"\n534:   [refl answer]\n535:   (swap! refl assoc\n536:          :source-descriptor (:dao.stream/descriptor answer)\n537:          :surface (conj (into #{} (:dao.stream.remote/surface answer))\n538:                         :closable)))\n539: \n540: \n541: (defn- next-age!\n542:   \"The next arrival age on the link: filed answers and installed\n543:    outcomes are aged in the order the link retained them.\"\n544:   [link]\n545:   (let [n (:filed-seq @link)]\n546:     (swap! link assoc :filed-seq (inc n))\n547:     n))\n548: \n549: \n550: (defn- evict-filed!\n551:   \"Bound the link's filed answers and installed outcomes together by\n552:    max-filed, evicting the oldest retained until within the bound. The\n553:    entry just filed is the newest, so filing an answer never evicts\n554:    that answer. Everything filed is idempotent-recomputable, so the\n555:    operation an evicted entry answered asks again; no outcome is\n556:    invented.\"\n557:   [link]\n558:   (when-some [m (:max-filed @link)]\n559:     (loop []\n560:       (let [{:keys [filed filed-cursors]} @link]\n561:         (when (< m (+ (count filed) (count filed-cursors)))\n562:           (let [aged (concat (map (fn [[id e]] [(:age e) :filed id]) filed)\n563:                              (map (fn [[k e]] [(:age e) :filed-cursors k])\n564:                                   filed-cursors))\n565:                 [_ where k] (apply min-key first aged)]\n566:             (swap! link update where dissoc k)\n567:             (recur)))))))\n568: \n569: \n570: (defn- file!\n571:   \"File answer `v` under `id` with the request it was sent for and the\n572:    reflection that sent it, as the newest retained entry, then bound\n573:    the retained entries by max-filed.\"\n574:   [link id req v refl]\n575:   (swap! link assoc-in [:filed id]\n576:          {:req req :ans v :reflection refl :age (next-age! link)})\n577:   (evict-filed! link))\n578: \n579: \n580: (defn- install-more!\n581:   \"Install each more outcome under the answer's served identity and at\n582:    the cursor that precedes it, so a later next at that cursor by a\n583:    reflection of the same stream returns the source's own outcome\n584:    without a request. The identity is half of the key: two served\n585:    identities can carry equal cursor values, and an outcome belongs to\n586:    its own stream. At most the link's stamped budget k less one are\n587:    installed -- the answer itself is the first of k -- and none when\n588:    the link stamped no budget: the surplus a peer sends is dropped.\n589:    Prefetch only fills free retained capacity: with max-filed, no more\n590:    are installed than fit beside what is already retained, so a\n591:    prefetch never evicts anything, its own answer included.\"\n592:   [link answer]\n593:   (let [identity (:dao.stream/identity answer)\n594:         k (stamped-budget link)\n595:         asked (if (and (integer? k) (pos? k)) (dec k) 0)\n596:         {:keys [max-filed filed filed-cursors]} @link\n597:         fits (if max-filed\n598:                (max 0 (- max-filed (count filed) (count filed-cursors)))\n599:                asked)]\n600:     (loop [cur (:dao.stream/cursor answer)\n601:            more (take (min asked fits) (:dao.stream.remote/more answer))]\n602:       (when (and cur (seq more))\n603:         (let [[o & further] more]\n604:           (swap! link assoc-in [:filed-cursors [identity cur]]\n605:                  {:outcome o :age (next-age! link)})\n606:           (recur (:dao.stream/cursor o) further))))))\n607: \n608: \n609: (defn- absorb-named!\n610:   \"A resolve's answer, read off the channel: taken only when it echoes\n611:    the name its outstanding request asked, and filed under its id for\n612:    the resolve that asked. No reflection exists for a name, so nothing\n613:    is marked gone and nothing is emitted. An answer that does not echo\n614:    the name never completes the request, which stays outstanding.\"\n615:   [link id entry v]\n616:   (let [req (:req entry)]\n617:     (when (and (named? v)\n618:                (= (:dao.stream.remote/name req)\n619:                   (:dao.stream.remote/name v)))\n620:       (swap! link update :outstanding dissoc id)\n621:       (file! link id req v nil))))\n622: \n623: \n624: (defn- absorb!\n625:   \"Consume one value read off the channel. A well-formed answer whose\n626:    id is outstanding and whose identity is the outstanding entry's\n627:    reflection's own identity is taken: a not-found error marks the\n628:    reflection gone; the attach probe's ok records the source's\n629:    descriptor and declared surface; an append!'s source outcome is\n630:    emitted on the event writer, correlated by id; any other answer is\n631:    filed under its id and its more outcomes installed. Answers whose\n632:    id is not outstanding, answers whose identity is not the\n633:    reflection's own -- a mismatch never completes a request, which\n634:    stays outstanding, and an answer that carries no identity\n635:    completes no identity request -- and values that are not\n636:    well-formed answers,\n637:    are dropped as diagnostics. The answer to a named request is the\n638:    resolve's (absorb-named!).\"\n639:   [link v]\n640:   (when (well-formed-answer? v)\n641:     (let [id (:dao.stream.remote/id v)]\n642:       (when-some [entry (get (:outstanding @link) id)]\n643:         (if (named? (:req entry))\n644:           (absorb-named! link id entry v)\n645:           (let [refl (:reflection entry)\n646:                 req (:req entry)\n647:                 op (:dao.stream.remote/op req)\n648:                 e (:dao.stream.remote/error v)]\n649:             (when (and (contains? v :dao.stream/identity)\n650:                        (= (:dao.stream/identity v) (:identity @refl)))\n651:               (swap! link update :outstanding dissoc id)\n652:               (swap! refl update :ids disj id)\n653:               (cond\n654:                 (= :dao.stream.remote/not-found e)\n655:                 (do (swap! refl assoc :gone? true)\n656:                     (when (or (= :dao.stream/descriptor op)\n657:                               (= :dao.stream/append! op))\n658:                       (emit! link v)))\n659: \n660:                 (= :dao.stream/descriptor op)\n661:                 ;; The attach probe's confirmation. ok records; a\n662:                 ;; no-surface or oversize error marks nothing.\n663:                 (when (nil? e)\n664:                   (learn! refl v)\n665:                   (emit! link v))\n666: \n667:                 (= :dao.stream/append! op)\n668:                 (emit! link v)\n669: \n670:                 :else\n671:                 (do (file! link id req v refl)\n672:                     (install-more! link v))))))))))\n673: \n674: \n675: (defn- channel-loss!\n676:   \"The channel reader answered end: the channel is gone. The link\n677:    abandons its outstanding ids, reporting each abandoned append! on\n678:    the event writer as append-unknown; filed answers are kept and\n679:    still returned; reattachment is the caller's policy.\"\n680:   [link]\n681:   (doseq [[id entry] (:outstanding @link)]\n682:     (when (= :dao.stream/append! (:dao.stream.remote/op (:req entry)))\n683:       (emit! link {:dao.stream.remote/event\n684:                    :dao.stream.remote/append-unknown\n685:                    :dao.stream.remote/id id}))\n686:     (when-some [refl (:reflection entry)]\n687:       (swap! refl update :ids disj id)))\n688:   (swap! link assoc :outstanding {} :channel-gone? true))\n689: \n690: \n691: (defn- retry-pending!\n692:   \"One more try of each probe the writer has refused, once per drain,\n693:    until a send is accepted; the accepted send is registered as the\n694:    outstanding probe and the normal filing path confirms it.\"\n695:   [link]\n696:   (doseq [[_ e] (:pending @link)]\n697:     (send-request! link (:reflection e) (:req e))))\n698: \n699: \n700: (defn- admit-probe!\n701:   \"Offer `refl`'s unadmitted attach probe to its link again: a probe\n702:    the link had no room to keep waits on its own reflection, so the\n703:    link's kept state stays within max-outstanding, and is sent, kept,\n704:    or left waiting by send-request! as on attach.\"\n705:   [refl]\n706:   (let [{:keys [probe link closed?]} @refl]\n707:     (when (and probe (not closed?) (not (:channel-gone? @link)))\n708:       (send-request! link refl probe))))\n709: \n710: \n711: (defn- drain!\n712:   \"Read the link's channel reader to blocked, filing each answer: the\n713:    caller's own polling is the cadence and no driver step exists. An\n714:    end is the channel's loss; a gap adopts the reader's own recovery\n715:    cursor, the lost wire values being lost. Each drain is also one\n716:    further ask of an outstanding descriptor probe -- the probe's\n717:    caller never asks it remotely, where a named request's caller asks\n718:    by calling resolve again -- so resend-after re-sends it, and\n719:    one more try of each probe the writer has refused, until a send\n720:    is accepted. With a drain-budget, at most that many reads -- ok and\n721:    gap alike -- are taken per drain, the link's cursor kept where it\n722:    stopped for the next operation's drain.\"\n723:   [link]\n724:   (when-not (:channel-gone? @link)\n725:     (doseq [[_ e] (:outstanding @link)]\n726:       (when (and (= :dao.stream/descriptor (:dao.stream.remote/op (:req e)))\n727:                  (not (named? (:req e))))\n728:         (count-ask! link (:dao.stream.remote/id (:req e)))))\n729:     (retry-pending! link)\n730:     (loop [remaining (:drain-budget @link)]\n731:       (when-not (and remaining (zero? remaining))\n732:         (let [r (stream/next (:reader @link) (:cursor @link))]\n733:           (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n734:             :dao.stream/ok\n735:             (do (absorb! link (:dao.stream/value r))\n736:                 (swap! link assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n737:                 (recur (when remaining (dec remaining))))\n738:             :dao.stream/blocked nil\n739:             :dao.stream/end (channel-loss! link)\n740:             :dao.stream/gap\n741:             (do (swap! link assoc :cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r)) nil)\n742:             nil))))))\n743: \n744: \n745: ;; =============================================================================\n746: ;; The reflection (2.4)\n747: ;; =============================================================================\n748: \n749: (defn- result\n750:   [outcome]\n751:   {:dao.stream/outcome outcome})\n752: \n753: \n754: (defn- refl-descriptor\n755:   \"Local: ok with the remote descriptor the reflection was attached\n756:    with and the identity -- the same identity as the source's own\n757:    descriptor, different reachability. A name outlives what it named:\n758:    descriptor still answers ok once gone, once closed, and after\n759:    channel loss.\"\n760:   [refl]\n761:   (drain! (:link @refl))\n762:   (admit-probe! refl)\n763:   {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n764:    :dao.stream/descriptor (:descriptor @refl)\n765:    :dao.stream/identity (:identity @refl)})\n766: \n767: \n768: (defn- surface-lacks?\n769:   \"True when the source's declared surface is learned and lacks the\n770:    surface `op` needs. Before the probe's answer the reflection\n771:    declares #{:reader :writer :closable}, so every operation is\n772:    attempted; an operation the source turns out to lack is answered as\n773:    the no-surface case.\"\n774:   [refl op]\n775:   (let [s (:surface @refl)]\n776:     (and (some? s) (not (contains? s (required-surface op))))))\n777: \n778: \n779: (defn- filed-answer-outcome\n780:   \"The outcome a filed answer yields: a protocol error translated per\n781:    the rules, otherwise the source's outcome map verbatim.\"\n782:   [ans]\n783:   (or (some-> (:dao.stream.remote/error ans) translated)\n784:       (bare-outcome ans)))\n785: \n786: \n787: (defn- filed-cursor\n788:   \"A filed answer for anchor `a` sent by `refl`, returned without\n789:    being forgotten: minting is idempotent, so the answer stays as true\n790:    as when it was minted.\"\n791:   [link refl a]\n792:   (when-some [[_ entry] (filed-for link refl :dao.stream/cursor a)]\n793:     (filed-answer-outcome (:ans entry))))\n794: \n795: \n796: (defn- filed-next!\n797:   \"A filed answer for cursor `c` sent by `refl`: the outcome an\n798:    installed more element put at `c` for the stream `refl` serves,\n799:    else the filed answer of a next request for `c`; returned and\n800:    forgotten.\"\n801:   [link refl c]\n802:   (let [k [(:identity @refl) c]]\n803:     (or (when-some [o (get (:filed-cursors @link) k)]\n804:           (swap! link update :filed-cursors dissoc k)\n805:           (filed-answer-outcome (:outcome o)))\n806:         (when-some [[id entry]\n807:                     (filed-for link refl :dao.stream/next c)]\n808:           (swap! link update :filed dissoc id)\n809:           (filed-answer-outcome (:ans entry))))))\n810: \n811: \n812: (defn- retry-read\n813:   \"The answer a just-sent cursor request gives: the source's map,\n814:    invalid-anchor included, arrives later as an answer.\"\n815:   []\n816:   {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n817:    :dao.stream/retry? true})\n818: \n819: \n820: (defn- send-or-count!\n821:   \"Send the request for `op` with `arg` when none of this reflection's\n822:    own is outstanding; otherwise count one further ask of the\n823:    outstanding request, which re-sends it at the link's resend-after\n824:    k.\"\n825:   [link refl op arg]\n826:   (if-some [id (outstanding-for link refl op arg)]\n827:     (count-ask! link id)\n828:     (send-request! link refl (wire-request link refl op [arg]))))\n829: \n830: \n831: (defn- refl-cursor\n832:   \"The cursor operation: a filed answer for the anchor is returned,\n833:    and a filed protocol error translated; otherwise a cursor request\n834:    is sent if none is outstanding, and the answer is transport-error\n835:    with :dao.stream/retry? true. Once closed, cursor answers closed;\n836:    once gone, transport-error naming not-found.\"\n837:   [refl a]\n838:   (let [link (:link @refl)]\n839:     (drain! link)\n840:     (admit-probe! refl)\n841:     (cond\n842:       (:closed? @refl) (result :dao.stream/closed)\n843:       (:gone? @refl) (translated :dao.stream.remote/not-found)\n844:       (surface-lacks? refl :dao.stream/cursor)\n845:       (translated :dao.stream.remote/no-surface)\n846:       :else\n847:       (or (filed-cursor link refl a)\n848:           (when-not (:channel-gone? @link)\n849:             (send-or-count! link refl :dao.stream/cursor a)\n850:             (retry-read))\n851:           (translated :dao.stream.remote/channel-gone)))))\n852: \n853: \n854: (defn- refl-next\n855:   \"The next operation: a filed answer for the cursor is returned and\n856:    forgotten; otherwise a next request is sent if none is outstanding,\n857:    and the answer is blocked -- nothing is observable at this position\n858:    through this handle yet. After close, filed outcomes then end. The\n859:    reflection never judges a cursor: cursor-mismatch and\n860:    invalid-cursor are only ever relayed from the source.\"\n861:   [refl c]\n862:   (let [link (:link @refl)]\n863:     (drain! link)\n864:     (admit-probe! refl)\n865:     (cond\n866:       (:closed? @refl)\n867:       (or (filed-next! link refl c) (result :dao.stream/end))\n868: \n869:       (:gone? @refl) (translated :dao.stream.remote/not-found)\n870: \n871:       (surface-lacks? refl :dao.stream/next)\n872:       (translated :dao.stream.remote/no-surface)\n873: \n874:       :else\n875:       (or (filed-next! link refl c)\n876:           (when-not (:channel-gone? @link)\n877:             (send-or-count! link refl :dao.stream/next c)\n878:             (result :dao.stream/blocked))\n879:           (translated :dao.stream.remote/channel-gone)))))\n880: \n881: \n882: (defn- refl-append\n883:   \"The append! operation: send the request and return the channel\n884:    writer's outcome -- ok is acceptance on the outbound path, exactly\n885:    the contract's Writing rule for a transport that carries values\n886:    toward a stream elsewhere. The source's outcome is emitted on the\n887:    event writer when it is filed, correlated by id; append! never\n888:    answers the source's full. Only an accepted send is in flight: a\n889:    refused append! never crossed, so its effect is not unknown; a send\n890:    over max-outstanding answers full, nothing crossing.\"\n891:   [refl v]\n892:   (let [link (:link @refl)]\n893:     (drain! link)\n894:     (admit-probe! refl)\n895:     (cond\n896:       (:closed? @refl) (result :dao.stream/closed)\n897:       (:gone? @refl) (translated :dao.stream.remote/not-found)\n898:       (surface-lacks? refl :dao.stream/append!)\n899:       (translated :dao.stream.remote/no-surface)\n900:       :else\n901:       (let [req (wire-request link refl :dao.stream/append! [v])\n902:             r (send! link req)]\n903:         (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n904:           (register! link refl req))\n905:         r))))\n906: \n907: \n908: (defn- refl-close\n909:   \"The close! operation, local: the reflection forgets its\n910:    outstanding ids and its kept, unsent probe, reporting each\n911:    outstanding append! on the event writer as append-unknown -- an\n912:    append whose answer never arrives has unknown effect; afterwards\n913:    append! answers closed, cursor answers closed, next answers filed\n914:    outcomes then end, and nothing crosses the wire. Idempotent, per\n915:    the contract's Close.\"\n916:   [refl]\n917:   (let [link (:link @refl)]\n918:     (swap! link update :pending\n919:            (fn [kept]\n920:              (into {}\n921:                    (remove (fn [[_ e]]\n922:                              (= refl (:reflection e)))\n923:                            kept))))\n924:     (swap! refl dissoc :probe)\n925:     (drain! link)\n926:     (when-not (:closed? @refl)\n927:       (doseq [id (:ids @refl)]\n928:         (when-some [entry (get (:outstanding @link) id)]\n929:           (when (= :dao.stream/append! (:dao.stream.remote/op (:req entry)))\n930:             (emit! link {:dao.stream.remote/event\n931:                          :dao.stream.remote/append-unknown\n932:                          :dao.stream.remote/id id}))\n933:           (swap! link update :outstanding dissoc id)))\n934:       (swap! refl assoc :closed? true :ids #{}))\n935:     (result :dao.stream/ok)))\n936: \n937: \n938: ;; =============================================================================\n939: ;; The link's resolve (2.4)\n940: ;; =============================================================================\n941: \n942: (defn- named-id\n943:   \"The least id in `entries` -- the link's outstanding or filed map --\n944:    whose request is a named request for the name `n`, if any.\"\n945:   [entries n]\n946:   (first\n947:     (sort\n948:       (keep (fn [[id e]]\n949:               (let [r (:req e)]\n950:                 (when (and (named? r) (= n (:dao.stream.remote/name r)))\n951:                   id)))\n952:             entries))))\n953: \n954: \n955: (defn- send-named!\n956:   \"Append one named descriptor request for `n` to the channel writer,\n957:    outstanding only when the writer accepted the send: a refused send\n958:    leaves the request unsent and the next resolve sends again. The\n959:    request carries the name in place of :dao.stream/identity.\"\n960:   [link n]\n961:   (let [req {:dao.stream.remote/name n\n962:              :dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/descriptor\n963:              :dao.stream.remote/args []\n964:              :dao.stream.remote/id (mint-id! link)}\n965:         r (send! link req)]\n966:     (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n967:       (swap! link assoc-in [:outstanding (:dao.stream.remote/id req)]\n968:              {:req req :asks 0 :reflection nil}))\n969:     r))\n970: \n971: \n972: (defn- resolved\n973:   \"The outcome a filed answer to a named request yields: ok with the\n974:    remote descriptor of the stream the name mapped to -- its own\n975:    identity, over this link's channel -- and the entry's declared\n976:    surface; a protocol error translated per the reflection's rules,\n977:    not-found included; any other outcome the source's own map.\"\n978:   [link ans]\n979:   (cond\n980:     (some? (:dao.stream.remote/error ans))\n981:     (translated (:dao.stream.remote/error ans))\n982: \n983:     (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome ans))\n984:     (let [identity (:dao.stream/identity ans)]\n985:       {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n986:        :dao.stream/descriptor {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/remote\n987:                                :dao.stream/identity identity\n988:                                :dao.stream/channel (:channel @link)}\n989:        :dao.stream/identity identity\n990:        :dao.stream.remote/surface (:dao.stream.remote/surface ans)})\n991: \n992:     :else\n993:     (dissoc (bare-outcome ans)\n994:             :dao.stream.remote/name :dao.stream.remote/surface)))\n995: \n996: \n997: (defn- resolve-name\n998:   \"The link's resolve: drain, then a filed answer for the name is\n999:    returned and forgotten -- a name is looked up afresh each time it\n1000:    is asked, never remembered. Otherwise a named descriptor request is\n1001:    sent if none is outstanding, and the answer is transport-error with\n1002:    :dao.stream/retry? true, as cursor answers. A send the writer\n1003:    refuses with full is retried by the next resolve; any other refusal\n1004:    is the writer's own outcome, leaves nothing outstanding and is\n1005:    remembered nowhere -- the writer is the source of truth for what it\n1006:    can carry -- so each resolve of that name attempts the send again.\n1007:    After channel loss the answer is transport-error naming\n1008:    channel-gone, not retryable.\"\n1009:   [link n]\n1010:   (drain! link)\n1011:   (if-some [id (named-id (:filed @link) n)]\n1012:     (let [ans (:ans (get (:filed @link) id))]\n1013:       (swap! link update :filed dissoc id)\n1014:       (resolved link ans))\n1015:     (cond\n1016:       (:channel-gone? @link)\n1017:       (translated :dao.stream.remote/channel-gone)\n1018: \n1019:       :else\n1020:       (if-some [id (named-id (:outstanding @link) n)]\n1021:         (do (count-ask! link id) (retry-read))\n1022:         (let [r (send-named! link n)]\n1023:           (if (contains? #{:dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/full}\n1024:                          (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n1025:             (retry-read)\n1026:             r))))))\n1027: \n1028: \n1029: (deftype ReflectionHandle\n1030:   [state]\n1031: \n1032:   stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n1033: \n1034:   (descriptor\n1035:     [_]\n1036:     (refl-descriptor state))\n1037: \n1038: \n1039:   stream/IDaoStreamReader\n1040: \n1041:   (cursor\n1042:     [_ anchor]\n1043:     (refl-cursor state anchor))\n1044: \n1045: \n1046:   (next\n1047:     [_ c]\n1048:     (refl-next state c))\n1049: \n1050: \n1051:   stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n1052: \n1053:   (append!\n1054:     [_ v]\n1055:     (refl-append state v))\n1056: \n1057: \n1058:   stream/IDaoStreamClosable\n1059: \n1060:   (close!\n1061:     [_]\n1062:     (refl-close state)))\n1063: \n1064: \n1065: ;; =============================================================================\n1066: ;; The remote descriptor dispatch (2.2)\n1067: ;; =============================================================================\n1068: \n1069: (defn- valid-remote-descriptor?\n1070:   \"A remote descriptor names a stream and a channel: the generic\n1071:    envelope rules, the :dao.stream/remote type, and a channel\n1072:    descriptor. It carries no authorization, no surface and no\n1073:    anchors; the mirror answers those.\"\n1074:   [d]\n1075:   (and (stream/valid-descriptor? d)\n1076:        (= :dao.stream/remote (:dao.stream/type d))\n1077:        (contains? d :dao.stream/channel)))\n1078: \n1079: \n1080: (defn links\n1081:   \"The asking side over one set of per-channel links: {:attach f\n1082:    :resolve g}. `f` is `attacher`'s entry. `(g channel-descriptor\n1083:    name)` is the link's resolve over the link `f` keeps for that\n1084:    channel, created here when none exists yet: a filed answer for the\n1085:    name is returned and forgotten -- ok with the remote descriptor of\n1086:    the stream the name maps to, its own identity over that channel,\n1087:    and the entry's declared surface under :dao.stream.remote/surface;\n1088:    the not-found error as transport-error with reason not-found;\n1089:    otherwise the named descriptor request is sent when none is\n1090:    outstanding and the answer is transport-error with\n1091:    :dao.stream/retry? true, as cursor answers. After channel loss the\n1092:    answer is transport-error naming channel-gone. A channel this peer\n1093:    does not reach is not-found. `opts` is `attacher`'s; a bound among\n1094:    them (:dao.stream.remote/drain-budget, max-outstanding, max-filed)\n1095:    that is neither nil nor a positive integer is a composition error.\"\n1096:   [opts]\n1097:   (let [channels (:dao.stream.remote/channels opts)\n1098:         policy (select-keys opts [:dao.stream.remote/events\n1099:                                   :dao.stream.remote/resend-after\n1100:                                   :dao.stream.remote/budget\n1101:                                   :dao.stream.remote/drain-budget\n1102:                                   :dao.stream.remote/max-outstanding\n1103:                                   :dao.stream.remote/max-filed])\n1104:         _ (when-not (every? #(pos-int-or-nil? (get policy %))\n1105:                             [:dao.stream.remote/drain-budget\n1106:                              :dao.stream.remote/max-outstanding\n1107:                              :dao.stream.remote/max-filed])\n1108:             (throw (ex-info \"invalid DaoStream remote link policy\"\n1109:                             {:policy policy})))\n1110:         by-channel (atom {})\n1111:         link-for! (fn [cd]\n1112:                     (swap! by-channel\n1113:                            (fn [m]\n1114:                              (if (contains? m cd)\n1115:                                m\n1116:                                (assoc m cd\n1117:                                       (new-link cd (get channels cd)\n1118:                                                 policy)))))\n1119:                     (get @by-channel cd))]\n1120:     {:attach\n1121:      (fn [descriptor]\n1122:        (if-not (valid-remote-descriptor? descriptor)\n1123:          (result :dao.stream/invalid-descriptor)\n1124:          (let [cd (:dao.stream/channel descriptor)]\n1125:            (if-not (contains? channels cd)\n1126:              (result :dao.stream/not-found)\n1127:              (let [link (link-for! cd)\n1128:                    refl (atom {:link link\n1129:                                :descriptor descriptor\n1130:                                :identity (:dao.stream/identity descriptor)\n1131:                                :surface nil\n1132:                                :source-descriptor nil\n1133:                                :gone? false\n1134:                                :closed? false\n1135:                                :ids #{}})]\n1136:                (send-request!\n1137:                  link refl\n1138:                  (wire-request link refl :dao.stream/descriptor []))\n1139:                {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n1140:                 :dao.stream/handle (ReflectionHandle. refl)\n1141:                 :dao.stream/attachment (str (random-uuid))})))))\n1142:      :resolve\n1143:      (fn [cd n]\n1144:        (if-not (contains? channels cd)\n1145:          (result :dao.stream/not-found)\n1146:          (resolve-name (link-for! cd) n)))}))\n1147: \n1148: \n1149: (defn attacher\n1150:   \"The composition's :dao.stream/attach entry for :dao.stream/remote\n1151:    descriptors; a dynamic dispatch table has this entry and no\n1152:    :dao.stream/create one, because attaching through this transport\n1153:    never creates. `opts` carries the composition data:\n1154:    :dao.stream.remote/channels maps each channel descriptor this peer\n1155:    reaches to its own end {:reader r :writer w} -- two ring buffers in\n1156:    one process today, the ws, udp and pair channels of section 3\n1157:    later; :dao.stream.remote/events is the optional event writer the\n1158:    links emit on; :dao.stream.remote/resend-after is the links'\n1159:    resend-after k, unbounded on an ordered reliable channel and small\n1160:    on udp; :dao.stream.remote/budget is the budget stamped on every\n1161:    next request; :dao.stream.remote/drain-budget bounds the reads per\n1162:    drain, :dao.stream.remote/max-outstanding the requests outstanding\n1163:    or kept per link, and :dao.stream.remote/max-filed the filed answers\n1164:    and installed outcomes per link, each nil for unbounded. One link is kept per channel descriptor, shared by\n1165:    every reflection through that channel. attach! answers ok at once\n1166:    with a reflection handle and a local, opaque\n1167:    :dao.stream/attachment -- the contract's deferred remote\n1168:    confirmation -- and the link sends one descriptor probe for the\n1169:    identity: its answer is the reflection's confirmation, not-found\n1170:    marking the reflection gone, ok recording the source's descriptor\n1171:    and declared surface. `links` gives the same entry with the link's\n1172:    resolve beside it.\"\n1173:   [opts]\n1174:   (:attach (links opts)))"}],"deferred":false}}
