line was 69/537, delta consistent with two new deftests). Should I accept without running? The task explicitly asks to run tests. Cannot in plan mode. My plan file will be the review report itself, plus a note that execution steps (test run + copy report to collab/) require exiting plan mode.\n\nActually — reconsidering: is there any way to run tests? shell_command is permission-gated and failed. No other execution tool. So no.\n\nAlso let me quickly check whether anything else in the diff might be problematic: per git status, modified files are docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md, src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc, src/cljc/dao/stream/ws_project.cljc, test/dao/stream/remote_test.cljc. Without git diff, can't see what exactly changed against HEAD, but commit e9645a2d was S2a and the S2b work (drain-budget, max-outstanding, max-filed, plus the reconcile) is the uncommitted diff. Reviewed current state of all relevant code paths. ws_project changes: mirror-bounds, step budgets etc — some were committed in S0/S1 (65f635d0 \"step budget, session cap, idle reaping on ws-project\"). Uncommitted ws_project changes are probably the dial policy select-keys for new keys. Verified current file contains them.\n\nAlso check that test file has no other new S2b tests I haven't looked at — sections at line 1815+ covered. counting-writer helper too — existing.\n\nMinor findings (non-blocking) for the report:\n1. `count-ask!`'s resend bypasses `send!` — but resends don't increase retained count so cap invariant holds; if writer is full at that moment, resend is silently dropped and asks resets — existing behavior, note only.\n2. Pending probes survive channel-loss! (not cleared) — bounded by cap, removed on close!/reflection ops; admit-probe! guards on channel-gone? so nothing sent. Cosmetic issue.\n3. Probes rejected with non-full outcomes (e.g., closed) are neither retained nor retried — confirmation deferred indefinitely for that reflection unless re-attached; consistent with doc since