ble clamp: `stamped-budget` = `min(budget, max-filed)` on the wire (mirror chase k=1 sends no `more` at all), and `install-more!` installs `min(k−1, free capacity)` so a surplus-sending peer still can't evict anything.\n- Eviction changed from lowest-id to arrival order (`:filed-seq`/`next-age!`); `file!` files newest-then-evicts-oldest, so filing never evicts itself. The lowest-id starvation route round 1 flagged is genuinely closed, and the deviation from the architect's ordering is **explicit** in the reconcile report and doc §2.4 (L294–299) — exactly what round 1 demanded.\n- `absorb!` order (`file!` then `install-more!`) keeps total ≤ max-filed with no second eviction; `evict-filed!` terminates.\n- Traced `a-prefetch-never-evicts-its-own-answer` (max-filed 1, budget 2): wire budget 1, blocked→serve→`:a`/`:b`/`:c` progression, retained ≤ 1 throughout. Round-1's perpetual-blocked repro cannot recur. The updated third row of `more-is-clamped-to-the-links-own-budget` (`1 1`, not `0 2`) also traces correct.\n\n## Docs & ws-project\n"}]}}
