{"type":"event","event":{"type":"message_update","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Even write_file is permission-gated. Which means in this session I can't write anything at all. I have no choice but to present the review verdict and findings inline as my response. Keep it structured but reasonably concise.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Even the plan-file write is permission-gated in this session, so I can't persist the report anywhere. Here is the complete review, ready to be saved to `collab/1791357700000-stream-s2b-review-r2.qwen3.8-max.findings.md` once writes are enabled.\n\n# S2b Round-2 Independent Review — Verdict: **ACCEPT**\n\nRead-only review of the uncommitted reconciliation on `stream-crossmachine-s2` @ `e9645a2d`. I hand-traced both fixes and both new tests line-by-line against the implementation.\n\n## P1-1: probe cap deadlock — resolved\n- `room?` (remote.cljc:408) admits only when `outstanding + (pending − self) < max-outstanding`, and both `send!` and the probe-retention branch of `send-request!` (L451–457) require it → invariant `outstanding + pending ≤ cap` holds on every path.\n- A kept probe's retry excludes itself, so it always sees ≤ cap−1 and always has room; only the writer can refuse it. Round-1's mutual-counting deadlock is structurally impossible.\n- No-room probes wait on their own reflection (`:probe`), re-offered by `admit-probe!` after `drain!` in all four ops (L762, 840, 864, 893); `refl-close` clears pending + `:probe` before draining; `channel-gone?`/`closed?` guarded.\n- No double-send interleaving: any accepting path clears both `:pending` and `:probe` markers, and `retry-pending!` runs before the absorb loop within a drain.\n- Traced `attach-probes-share-a-capped-link` both cases (cap 1 accepting; cap 2 with `full-then-forward-writer 3`, counting all 5 writer appends and c's local refusal) — every assertion matches the trace, ending at held 0, all confirmed.\n\n## P1-2: prefetch self-eviction — resolved\n- Double clamp: `stamped-budget` = `min(budget, max-filed)` on the wire (mirror chase k=1 sends no `more` at all), and `install-more!` installs `min(k−1, free capacity)` so a surplus-sending peer still can't evict anything.\n- Eviction changed from lowest-id to arrival order (`:filed-seq`/`next-age!`); `file!` files newest-then-evicts-oldest, so filing never evicts itself. The lowest-id starvation route round 1 flagged is genuinely closed, and the deviation from the architect's ordering is **explicit** in the reconcile report and doc §2.4 (L294–299) — exactly what round 1 demanded.\n- `absorb!` order (`file!` then `install-more!`) keeps total ≤ max-filed with no second eviction; `evict-filed!` terminates.\n- Traced `a-prefetch-never-evicts-its-own-answer` (max-filed 1, budget 2): wire budget 1, blocked→serve→`:a`/`:b`/`:c` progression, retained ≤ 1 throughout. Round-1's perpetual-blocked repro cannot recur. The updated third row of `more-is-clamped-to-the-links-own-budget` (`1 1`, not `0 2`) also traces correct.\n\n## Docs & ws-project\n§2.4 bullets match the implementation exactly (refusal outcome mappings, room rule, invariant, probe-on-reflection, arrival-order eviction, stamped budget ≤ max-filed). `ws_project.cljc` `dial` propagates both new keys via policy select-keys (L481–486).\n\n## Non-blocking notes\n1. `count-ask!` resend bypasses `send!` — safe (retained count unchanged), pre-existing.\n2. A probe refused with non-`full` (e.g. closed) is neither kept nor retried — channel is effectively gone anyway.\n3. `:pending` survives `channel-loss!` — bounded, inert, cleared by `close!`. Cosmetic.\n4. Test message \"the source's own blocked\" is really the reflection's pending-send blocked. Trivial.\n\n## Verification caveat\nThe"}]}}
