ge!`); `file!` files newest-then-evicts-oldest, so filing never evicts itself. The lowest-id starvation route round 1 flagged is genuinely closed, and the deviation from the architect's ordering is **explicit** in the reconcile report and doc §2.4 (L294–299) — exactly what round 1 demanded.\n- `absorb!` order (`file!` then `install-more!`) keeps total ≤ max-filed with no second eviction; `evict-filed!` terminates.\n- Traced `a-prefetch-never-evicts-its-own-answer` (max-filed 1, budget 2): wire budget 1, blocked→serve→`:a`/`:b`/`:c` progression, retained ≤ 1 throughout. Round-1's perpetual-blocked repro cannot recur. The updated third row of `more-is-clamped-to-the-links-own-budget` (`1 1`, not `0 2`) also traces correct.\n\n## Docs & ws-project\n§2.4 bullets match the implementation exactly (refusal outcome mappings, room rule, invariant, probe-on-reflection, arrival-order eviction, stamped budget ≤ max-filed). `ws_project.cljc` `dial` propagates both new keys via policy select-keys (L481–486).\n\n## Non-blocking notes\n1. `count-ask!` resend bypasses `send!` — safe (retained count unchanged), pre-existing.\n2. A probe refused with non-`full` (e.g. closed) is neither kept nor retried — channel is effectively gone anyway.\n3. `:pending` survives `channel-loss!` — bounded, inert, cleared by `close!`. Cosmetic.\n4. Test message \"the source's own blocked\" is really the reflection's pending-send blocked. Trivial.\n\n## Verification caveat\nThe test suite could **not** be run in this session — both `shell_command` and `write_file` are permission-gated (plan mode without `--yolo`). The implementer reports 71 tests / 565 assertions / 0 failures; round-1 baseline was 69/537, and the delta is consistent with exactly the two added deftests. Before finalizing, run `clojure -M:test -n dao.stream.remote-test -n dao.stream.ws-project-test` in the worktree and save this report to the collab path.","stopReason":"end_turn","turnCount":13,"usage":{"inputTokens":565401,"outputTokens":21680,"cacheReadTokens":482176,"cacheWriteTokens":0},"systemPromptTokens":null,"nextState":{"sessionId":"82952d8f-66d8-4b3e-b13e-2d32e4842155","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created-GMT: 2026-10-07 07:21:00 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-07 14:21:00 Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh\nCoding-Agent: cmd\nSession-ID: unavailable\n\n# Task: stream-crossmachine-s2b-review-r2\nRole: Independent Code Reviewer\nImplementers:\n- Model: qwen/qwen3.8-max | Assigned: 1791357700000 | Status: active | Rationale: Independent code review of Slice S2b Round 2 (reallocated to Command Code qwen/qwen3.8-max per owner directive re: codex quota).\n\n## Review Instructions\nYou are the independent code reviewer for Datomworld.\nWork exclusively inside the dedicated feature worktree:\n`/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2` (branch `stream-crossmachine-s2` @ `e9645a2d`).\nDO NOT EDIT ANY CODE OR TEST FILES. READ-ONLY REVIEW.\n\n### Context\nIn Round 1, independent review requested changes on:\n1. P1: Refused attach probes exceeded `max-outstanding` and deadlocked retries.\n2. P1: Prefetch eviction made ordinary `next` requests permanently blocked (`max-filed 1`, `budget 2`).\n\nThe implementer (Claude Opus 5-5) reconciled both:\n- In `src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc`:\n  1. Refused attach probes are only retained in `:pending` if there is space under `max-outstanding`. Probes with no room wait on their own reflection and are retried on the reflection's subsequent operations, eliminating probe retry deadlock.\n  2. Prefetched `more` outcomes only fill free retained capacity and never evict the primary answer. The request budget sent with `next` is clamped to `max-filed`. Eviction order is FIFO (arrival order) rather than lowest ID, preventing an answer from evicting itself upon storage.\n- In `test/dao/stream/remote_test.cljc`:\n  - Added regression test `attach-probes-share-a-capped-link` (testing 3 reflections sharing cap 1 and cap 2).\n  - Added regression test `a-prefetch-never-evicts-its-own-answer` (testing single reader progress with `max-filed 1`, `budget 2`).\n- Updated `docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md` §2.4.\n\n### Verification to Perform\n- Inspect the full uncommitted diff (`git diff`).\n- Check that the two P1 defects are thoroughly resolved with zero regression hazards.\n- Run `clojure -M:test -n dao.stream.remote-test -n dao.stream.ws-project-test` (71 tests, 565 assertions).\n- State your verdict (ACCEPT / CHANGES REQUESTED) and detailed findings.\n\nWrite your report directly to:\n`collab/1791357700000-stream-s2b-review-r2.qwen3.8-max.findings.md`"}],"meta":{"source":"user","createdAt":1791357630193,"messageId":"a471dccf-5107-4cdf-a1a1-930e7d366848"}},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is a review task, but I'm in PLAN MODE. Plan mode is read-only and only permits writing to ~/.commandcode/plans/. This task asks me to write a findings file to collab/ and run tests (read-only commands are fine, but clojure test execution is… actually running tests doesn't modify code, but does it create target directories? Test execution is generally close to read-only, but plan mode says non-read-only tools are prohibited).\n\nContradiction: plan mode overrides other instructions. Writing the findings file to collab/ is not permitted. Running tests via shell — in plan mode, commands that change state are not permitted. Running clojure tests writes compilation artifacts. Hmm.\n\nBut the role of plan mode is: explore, design, write a plan. The user's task is a review task. In plan mode I should do the review analysis (read-only), write the plan, and explain that the findings file cannot be written. Alternatively, I could perform the review within my response and write a plan describing that the findings report should be written after exiting plan mode.\n\nActually, a reasonable approach: do the read-only review work (read diffs, code, tests), and possibly run the test suite (which is borderline; running te