can't see what exactly changed against HEAD, but commit e9645a2d was S2a and the S2b work (drain-budget, max-outstanding, max-filed, plus the reconcile) is the uncommitted diff. Reviewed current state of all relevant code paths. ws_project changes: mirror-bounds, step budgets etc — some were committed in S0/S1 (65f635d0 \"step budget, session cap, idle reaping on ws-project\"). Uncommitted ws_project changes are probably the dial policy select-keys for new keys. Verified current file contains them.\n\nAlso check that test file has no other new S2b tests I haven't looked at — sections at line 1815+ covered. counting-writer helper too — existing.\n\nMinor findings (non-blocking) for the report:\n1. `count-ask!`'s resend bypasses `send!` — but resends don't increase retained count so cap invariant holds; if writer is full at that moment, resend is silently dropped and asks resets — existing behavior, note only.\n2. Pending probes survive channel-loss! (not cleared) — bounded by cap, removed on close!/reflection ops; admit-probe! guards on channel-gone? so nothing sent. Cosmetic issue.\n3. Probes rejected with non-full outcomes (e.g., closed) are neither retained nor retried — confirmation deferred indefinitely for that reflection unless re-attached; consistent with doc since channel is effectively gone.\n4. Final assertion message in `a-prefetch-never-evicts-its-own-answer` says \"source's own blocked\" but it's the reflection's pending-send blocked; trivial.\n5. Could not run the suite in this session (shell gated); static trace of both new tests against implementation confirms the logic; counts consistent with implementer's reported 71/565.\n\nEviction order deviation (arrival vs lowest id) is explicit in reconcile report and doc — round 1 review required exactly this (\"any necessary changes to the eviction order stated by the architect should be made explicit\"). ✓ Satisfied.\n\nNow let me write the plan file. Plan file location: ~/.commandcode/plans/. Absolute path needed — ~ expansion: /Users/sto/.commandcode/plans/stream-s2b-review-r2-findings.md. Instructions say use full absolute path starting with ~/. Write to \"/Users/sto/.commandcode/plans/stream-s2b-review-r2-findings.md\"... instructions say \"~/.commandcode/plans/\" — use ~-prefixed path literally? \"ALWAYS use full absolute paths starting with ~/\". OK, use \"~/.commandcode/plans/stream-s2b-review-r2-findings.md\".\n\nPlan will contain: verdict ACCEPT, detailed findings, and execution steps (write findings file to collab/ path, run test command, report results).\n\nWith this, I've now got a complete picture of the whole thing. I statically traced both P1 fixes against the two new regression tests and the documentation — since shell execution is locked down in this session (plan mode + permission gate), I can't run the test suite or do `git diff` here. I'll write up the full review report as a plan file, together with the execution steps for finalizing it.\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_9aadadd679d34a13a7697f39","name":"write_file","input":{"file_path":"~/.commandcode/plans/stream-s2b-review-r2-findings.md","content":"# Plan: Deliver S2b Round-2 review report (verdict: ACCEPT)\n\n## Context\nTask `stream-crossmachine-s2b-review-r2`: independent read-only review of the S2b\nreconciliation on branch `stream-crossmachine-s2` @ `e9645a2d` (worktree\n`/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2`). The review analysis is COMPLETE\n(static trace of code + both new tests + doc). What remains is blocked by plan\nmode: writing the report to `collab/` and running the test suite.\n\n## Verdict: ACCEPT\n\n## Review findings (the report body)\n\n### P1-1 (probe deadlock) — resolved\n`src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc`:\n- New `room?` (L408–418) admits a request only when\n  `outstanding + (pending − self) < max-outstanding`. Both `send!` (L421–428,\n  local refusal as `full`, nothing crossing) and the probe-retention branch of\n  `send-request!` (L451–457) require it, so the invariant\n  `outstanding + pending ≤ max-outstanding` holds on every path.\n- Deadlock elimination traced: a kept probe's retry excludes itself from the\n  count, so with the invariant it always sees ≤ cap−1 and always has room;\n  only the writer itself can refuse it. Round-1's mutual-counting deadlock\n  (two pending probes at cap 1 each refusing the other) is structurally\n  impossible.\n- No-room recovery: the probe waits on its own reflection (`:probe`), offered\n  again by `admit-probe!` (L700–708) right after `drain!` in all four\n  reflection ops (descriptor L762, cursor L840, next L864, append! L893).\n  `refl-close` clears both the reflection's pending entries and `:probe`\n  (L918–924) before draining, so close cannot resurrect a probe.\n  `admit-probe!` guards `closed?` and `channel-gone?`.\n- No double-send interleaving: within one op, `drain!` runs `retry-pending!`\n  before the absorb loop; a successful send clears BOTH `:pending` entry and\n  `:probe` (L446–449), so `admit-probe!` afterwards is a no-op. A probe can\n  transiently sit in both `:pending` and `:probe` (retry refused for no room),\n  but every accepting path clears both markers atomically-enough under the\n  single-driver model. Traced against both test scenarios below.\n\nTest `attach-probes-share-a-capped-link` (test L1992–2031) — hand-traced both\ncases against the implementation:\n- Cap 1, accepting writer: attach a sends (held 1); b, c locally refused onto\n  their reflections (no writer consumption, probes-on-wire stays 1). Each\n  serve!+op admits exactly the next probe. All assertions match the trace;\n  final state: all confirmed, held 0.\n- Cap 2, `full-then-forward-writer 3`: a, b kept in `:pending` (at cap), c on\n  `:probe`. Writer refusals counted: a(full), b(full), a-retry(full),\n  b-retry(ok, outstanding), a-retry(ok, outstanding=2), c locally refused\n  (never appended) — matches assertions `(= 2 (count (:outstanding ...)))`,\n  `(<= (held link) 2)`, `:probe` presence/nil transitions, final held 0.\n\n### P1-2 (prefetch self-eviction) — resolved\n- `stamped-budget` (L384–392): `min(budget, max-filed)`; `wire-request` stamps\n  it on `next`, so the peer is never asked to chase outcomes the link would\n  drop. With max-filed 1 / budget 2 the wire budget is 1 → mirror chase k=1\n  returns no `more` at all (first clamp).\n- `install-more!` (L580–606): installs `min(budget−1, max-filed − filed −\n  filed-cursors)` — prefetch only fills free capacity, never evicts, even\n  against a surplus-sending peer (second, independent clamp).\n- Eviction order changed from lowest-id to arrival order (`:filed-seq` /\n  `next-age!`, L541–547); `file!` (L570–577) files as newest then\n  `evict-filed!` (L550–567) removes min-age until within bound, so filing\n  never evicts the answer just filed. The lowest-id hazard (re-asked answer\n  gets a lower id and evicts itself) is real and correctly identified in the\n  reconcile report; the deviation from the architect's stated ordering is\n  EXPLICIT in both the reconcile report and doc §2.4 L294–299 (\"in the order\n  the link retained them\"), which is what round-1 review demanded.\n- Ordering in `absorb!`: `file!` then `install-more!` (L671–672) — after\n  file!'s eviction the total is ≤ m, and `fits` guarantees install keeps it\n  ≤ m with no second eviction. Loop termination in `evict-filed!` is fine\n  (each pass removes one entry; m ≥ 1 by policy validation).\n\nTest `a-prefetch-never-evicts-its-own-answer` (L2034–2052) — traced: stamped\nwire budget asserted 1; each of next 0/1/2 goes blocked → serve! → returns\n:a/:b/:c; retained ≤ 1 after every step; the mid-loop `blocked` assertion at\nc>0 confirms nothing is prefetched past capacity. Round-1's reproduction\n(perpetual blocked with max-filed 1, budget 2) cannot recur: asked = 0 and\nfits = 0 both independently prevent the install.\n\nTest `more-is-clamped-to-the-links-own-budget` third row updated to\n`[{:budget 4 :max-filed 2} 1 1]` — traced: stamped 2, asked 1, fits\n2−1−0=1 → 1 filed + 1 installed. Correct; the old `0 2` expectation was the\ndefect.\n\n### Doc §2.4 (docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md L284–302)\nMatches the implementation exactly: local refusal outcome mappings\n(cursor/resolve → transport-error retry?, next → blocked, append! → full with\nknown effect), room-rule + invariant + probe-waits-on-reflection for\nmax-outstanding; arrival-order eviction, file-never-evicts-itself,\nprefetch-fills-free-capacity, stamped budget ≤ max-filed for max-filed.\n`ws_project.cljc` `dial` propagates max-outstanding/max-filed through the\npolicy select-keys (L481–486) — round-1 contract item confirmed.\n\n### Non-blocking notes (no action required)\n1. `count-ask!` resend (L473) bypasses `send!`; acceptable — a resend does not\n   grow the retained count, so the cap invariant is unaffected (pre-existing).\n2. A probe refused with a non-`full` outcome (e.g. closed writer) is neither\n   kept nor retried; in practice that means the channel is gone, and\n   confirmation is only observable through that reflection anyway.\n3. `:pending` probes survive `channel-loss!` (bounded by cap; cleared by\n   close!; `admit-probe!`/`drain!` guard on `channel-gone?` so nothing sends).\n   Cosmetic.\n4. Final assertion message in the prefetch test says \"the source's own\n   blocked\" though it is the reflection's pending-send blocked. Trivial.\n\n### Verification status\n- Static review: COMPLETE (full read of remote.cljc, ws_project.cljc, both new\n  tests + helpers, doc §2.4, round-1 findings, reconcile report).\n- Test suite: NOT RUN in this session — shell execution is permission-gated\n  (plan mode). Implementer reports 71 tests / 565 assertions / 0 failures;\n  round-1 baseline was 69/537, and the delta is consistent with exactly the\n  two added deftests. Must be re-run as an execution step below before the\n  report is finalized.\n\n## Execution steps (after plan approval / exiting plan mode)\n1. Run in `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2`:\n   `clojure -M:test -n dao.stream.remote-test -n dao.stream.ws-project-test`\n   — confirm 71 tests, 565 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors. If the run\n   contradicts the static verdict, amend the report before writing it.\n2. Write the report body above (verdict, findings, notes, and the actual test\n   output replacing the \"NOT RUN\" paragraph) to:\n   `collab/1791357700000-stream-s2b-review-r2.qwen3.8-max.findings.md`\n3. No code/test/doc edits — review is read-only per task contract.\n"}}],"meta":{"source":"model","createdAt":1791358241602,"messageId":"3e1672f8-f29c-4a8d-a7a9-4c996c806d9e"}},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_9aadadd679d34a13a7697f39","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Error: Tool \"write_file\" requires permissions. Use --yolo (or --dangerously-skip-permissions) to enable file writes and shell commands in print mode."}]}],"meta":{"source":"tool","messageId":"af365a8e-df38-4262-8609-0e5b7f48abb7"}},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Even write_file is permission-gated. Which means in this session I can't write anything at all. I have no choice but to present the review verdict and findings inline as my response. Keep it structured but reasonably concise.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Even the plan-file write is permission-gated in this session, so I can't persist the report anywhere. Here is the complete review, ready to be saved to `collab/1791357700000-stream-s2b-review-r2.qwen3.8-max.findings.md` once writes are enabled.\n\n# S2b Round-2 Independent Review — Verdict: **ACCEPT**\n\nRead-only review of the uncommitted reconciliation on `stream-crossmachine-s2` @ `e9645a2d`. I hand-traced both fixes and both new tests line-by-line against the implementation.\n\n## P1-1: probe cap deadlock — resolved\n- `room?` (remote.cljc:408) admits only when `outstanding + (pending − self) < max-outstanding`, and both `send!` and the probe-retention branch of `send-request!` (L451–457) require it → invariant `outstanding + pending ≤ cap` holds on every path.\n- A kept probe's retry excludes itself, so it always sees ≤ cap−1 and always has room; only the writer can refuse it. Round-1's mutual-counting deadlock is structurally impossible.\n- No-room probes wait on their own reflection (`:probe`), re-offered by `admit-probe!` after `drain!` in all four ops (L762, 840, 864, 893); `refl-close` clears pending + `:probe` before draining; `channel-gone?`/`closed?` guarded.\n- No double-send interleaving: any accepting path clears both `:pending` and `:probe` markers, and `retry-pending!` runs before the absorb loop within a drain.\n- Traced `attach-probes-share-a-capped-link` both cases (cap 1 accepting; cap 2 with `full-then-forward-writer 3`, counting all 5 writer appends and c's local refusal) — every assertion matches the trace, ending at held 0, all confirmed.\n\n## P1-2: prefetch self-eviction — resolved\n- Double clamp: `stamped-budget` = `min(budget, max-filed)` on the wire (mirror chase k=1 sends no `more` at all), and `install-more!` installs `min(k−1, free capacity)` so a surplus-sending peer still can't evict anything.\n- Eviction changed from lowest-id to arrival order (`:filed-seq`/`next-age!`); `file!` files newest-then-evicts-oldest, so filing never evicts itself. The lowest-id starvation route round 1 flagged is genuinely closed, and the deviation from the architect's ordering is **explicit** in the reconcile report and doc §2.4 (L294–299) — exactly what round 1 demanded.\n- `absorb!` order (`file!` then `install-more!`) keeps total ≤ max-filed with no second eviction; `evict-filed!` terminates.\n- Traced `a-prefetch-never-evicts-its-own-answer` (max-filed 1, budget 2): wire budget 1, blocked→serve→`:a`/`:b`/`:c` progression, retained ≤ 1 throughout. Round-1's perpetual-blocked repro cannot recur. The updated third row of `more-is-clamped-to-the-links-own-budget` (`1 1`, not `0 2`) also traces correct.\n\n## Docs & ws-project\n§2.4 bullets match the implementation exactly (refusal outcome mappings, room rule, invariant, probe-on-reflection, arrival-order eviction, stamped budget ≤ max-filed). `ws_project.cljc` `dial` propagates both new keys via policy select-keys (L481–486).\n\n## Non-blocking notes\n1. `count-ask!` resend bypasses `send!` — safe (retained count unchanged), pre-existing.\n2. A probe refused with non-`full` (e.g. closed) is neither kept nor retried — channel is effectively gone anyway.\n3. `:pending` survives `channel-loss!` — bounded, inert, cleared by `close!`. Cosmetic.\n4. Test message \"the source's own blocked\" is really the reflection's pending-send blocked. Trivial.\n\n## Verification caveat\nThe test suite could **not** be run in this session — both `shell_command` and `write_file` are permission-gated (plan mode without `--yolo`). The implementer reports 71 tests / 565 assertions / 0 failures; round-1 baseline was 69/537, and the delta is consistent with exactly the two added deftests. Before finalizing, run `clojure -M:test -n dao.stream.remote-test -n dao.stream.ws-project-test` in the worktree and save this report to the collab path."}],"meta":{"source":"model","createdAt":1791358283111,"messageId":"41b55810-453a-4c17-b1c5-f968936b98cd"}}],"interrupted":false,"modState":{"workspace":{"cwd":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-stream-s2","platform":"darwin","branch":"stream-crossmachine-s2","gitStatus":"M docs/design/dao.stream.remote.md\n M src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc\n M src/cljc/dao/stream/ws_project.cljc\n M test/dao/stream/remote_test.cljc\n?? collab/1791304310868-architect-transport-mob-consensus.gpt-6-astra.findings.md\n?? collab/1791305896793-stream-s0-s1.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md\n?? collab/1791305896793-stream-s0-s1.claude-opus-5-5.prompt.md\n?? collab/1791305896793-stream-s0-s1.claude-opus-5-5.stdout.log\n?? collab/1791306950355-stream-s0-s1-review.glm-5.3.findings.md\n?? collab/1791306950355-stream-s0-s1-review.glm-5